system capability table entry containing the base/limit\
values. The capability does however contain its own\
access type for the required block.\
    (3) The effect of the load capability instruction\
is to take the access field from the capability and\
the base/limit values from the system capability table\
and put them together in the required capability\
register.\
\
Capability Structure\
\
20. The concept of a capability as an access right to\
a store block may now be dissociated from the physical\
location of the block in the storage system. The\
system capability table is accessed automatically by\
the load capability instruction and the programmer\
need know nothing about it. He can imagine a capability\
register to have the same format as a stored capability,\
consisting of an access field and a block identity field\
(Fig. 4). Conceptually, a capability (access right)\
is loaded into a register when access to the corres-\
ponding block is required. Equally, a capability\
held in a register can be stored in a capability block\
until access is required to the block defined.\
