Capabilities for Parallel Devices\
\
27. A peripheral device interfaced to the peripheral\
buses has the appearance of a small store module\
(para. 8). Consequently, like any other block in the\
storage system, its register set is defined by a capa-\
bility, permitting it to be operated on by standard\
CPU instructions and protecting it against unauthorised\
access.\
\
\
OPERATING SYSTEM STRUCTURE\
\
28. The operating system is designed as a modular set\
of reentrant program packages which both run on and\
control a hardware configuration as described above.\
The broad structure of the operating system is depicted\
in Fig. 6 and its two parts:-\
